Speedy the Rollerskater for AmigaOS 3 - @RELEASE_VERSION@
==========================================================

Speedy the Rollerskater (Full Version) by SynfigMaster91, a free and open
source platform game made with the Open Surge Engine, with the Amiga
OpenSurge engine inside its drawer: unpack, install and play. Nothing else
needs installing first.

The author's terms (from the game's page and its README!!!.txt): "This game
is free and open source. It means you can share, study and modify/fix
something you don't like or you think it needs a fix. If you share or put
this game in somewhere, please give me credit." The credit is in CREDITS.

  https://sonicfangameshq.com/forums/showcase/speedy-the-rollerskater.977/

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-Speedy beside the Speedy drawer: it checks the CPU,
FPU and GFOpenGPU, asks where the Speedy drawer should go (Work:Games is
offered) and copies it there. Before that it offers to check game.zip
against the SHA-256 the archive was made with (game.zip.sha256), with
Tools/SHA256; that finds an archive damaged in the download or while it
was unpacked. The drawer also runs where it was unpacked.

What is in the drawer
---------------------
StartGame   starts the game
game.zip    the game's files, unchanged apart from what OpenSurge 0.6.1
            needs: the Windows program files are left out, the menu's
            MenuButtonList declaration is updated, a surge.cfg is added
game.zip.sha256  game.zip's SHA-256, for Install-Speedy's check
Engine/     the OpenSurge engine (below)
Tools/      SHA256, a small command that checks a SHA-256
CREDITS     who made the game, its art and its music
Licences/   licences, the game's own credits.txt and README!!!.txt

What it needs
-------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 (Installer 43.3 or newer for Install-Speedy)
- a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU
- GFOpenGPU: LIBS:GFOpenGPU/GL.module and SDL2.module (as on AmiCradle)
- about 300 MB free on the hard disk, and plenty of Fast RAM

The engine
----------
Engine/ is Amiga OpenSurge, Open Surge Engine 0.6.1.3 for AmigaOS 3,
exactly as released:

  release   @ENGINE_REPO@ @ENGINE_TAG@
  commit    @ENGINE_COMMIT@
  archive   @ENGINE_ASSET@
  sha256    @ENGINE_SHA256@
  program   Engine/opensurge
  sha256    @ENGINE_BINARY_SHA256@
  compiler  @ENGINE_COMPILER@

No separate engine install is needed: StartGame runs this copy. The engine
keeps its settings, logfile.txt and the game's compatibility pack in
Engine/ (Engine/.userdata). Licences/SOURCE.txt says where its source is.

Starting and playing
--------------------
Double-click StartGame in the Speedy drawer. From a Shell, CD to the
drawer first, then Execute StartGame. F10 switches between a window and
the full screen. Leave the game from its own menu (Esc brings it up in
most games).

Licences
--------
Licences/GPL-3.0.txt   the engine (GNU GPL 3 or later)
Licences/SOURCE.txt    where the engine's source is, at the exact commit
Licences/Port-scripts-MIT.txt  StartGame, the Installer script, Tools/
Licences/SHA256.txt    Tools/SHA256 (MIT, AmiCradle Team)
Engine/licenses/       the engine's own art, sound and font licences
game.zip licenses/    the game's own licence texts (inside game.zip)

The port's repository: https://github.com/DalsinAI/amigaspeedy
(port commit @PORT_COMMIT@)
